### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments API — PENDING CHECKOUT (POST /api/v1/orders with paymentProvider)
#
# How to run: VS Code REST Client — click "Send Request" top to bottom.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker stack up with the Payments module: docker compose up -d --build
#   - Seeded chain admin exists: admin@devtunde.com / Password123!
#   - SANDBOX KEYS in .env (see scripts/payments-sandbox-setup-wizard.sh):
#       PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY, MONNIFY_API_KEY, MONNIFY_SECRET_KEY,
#       MONNIFY_CONTRACT_CODE
#     Without the keys, every provider request answers 400
#     "payment-provider-not-configured" instead of 202 — that 400 is a
#     labeled state in this file too.
#
# Contract (ticket 0017):
#   - One door: POST /api/v1/orders + optional paymentProvider
#     (PAYSTACK | MONNIFY). Absent = counter-settled 201 PAID (0016).
#   - CASH is manual, forever: CASH + provider = 400.
#   - NO HOLDS: the shelf is untouched until verify settles the slip.
#   - Every order mints an order number (O-000001, zero-padded, chain-wide).
#   - The slip carries the provider details to show the customer:
#     paystack.authorizationUrl (hosted checkout) or
#     monnify.accountNumber / bankName / bankCode (reserved account).
#
# `# Expected:` labels the status each request proves.
# Tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup from the top.
# Captures are session-scoped: a "No value is resolved" error means
# re-send the setup requests from the top of this file.
# All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1 — Setup: chain admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: mint the store's seat admin (fresh persona per run)
# @name seatSignup
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Payments Seat Admin",
  "email": "pay-seat-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234581"
}

### 3 — Setup: seat admin logs in
# @name seatLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{seatSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: chain admin creates the store, seating that admin
# @name store
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Payments Probe Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{seatLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Probe Way",
    "phone": "08012345681",
    "email": "pay-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Setup: seat admin hires the primary cashier
# @name hire
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Payments Cashier",
  "email": "pay-cashier-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234582",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 6 — Setup: the cashier logs in
# @name cashierLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hire.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — Setup: the cashier opens a session
# @name session
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Setup: chain admin creates a category
# @name category
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Payments Probe Category {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 9 — Setup: the seat admin lists a product (₦12,000.00 selling price)
# @name listing
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/store/{{store.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Probe Milk 1L",
  "sku": "PROBE-PAY-{{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Payments probe item",
  "brand": "TestBrand",
  "image": "https://cdn.devtunde.com/item.png",
  "categoryPublicId": "{{category.response.body.publicId}}",
  "mrp": 15000.00,
  "sellingPrice": 12000.00
}

### 10 — Setup: stock the shelf (10 units)
# @name stock
# Expected: 201 — an OPENING movement is recorded
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
  "quantity": 10,
  "lowStockThreshold": 1
}

### 11 — THE HAPPY PATH: bank transfer via Paystack
# @name paystackSlip
# Expected: 202 — status PENDING_PAYMENT, provider PAYSTACK,
# orderNumber O-0000xx, paystack.authorizationUrl present, monnify absent,
# paidAt absent, expiresAt present. Stock UNCHANGED (no holds).
# (Without PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY in .env: 400 payment-provider-not-configured)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 12 — Bank transfer via Monnify: the slip carries the reserved account
# @name monnifySlip
# Expected: 202 — provider MONNIFY, monnify.accountNumber / bankName /
# bankCode present, paystack absent.
# (CARD + MONNIFY is a 400 — Monnify is the transfer rail — see case 27.)
# (Without the MONNIFY_* keys in .env: 400 payment-provider-not-configured)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "MONNIFY"
}

### 13 — Cash has no gateway: CASH + provider is refused
# Expected: 400 — cash-gateway-not-allowed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 14 — A provider outside PAYSTACK/MONNIFY
# Expected: 400 — checkout-invalid
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "FLUTTERWAVE"
}

### 15 — No provider at all: the 0016 counter path is untouched
# Expected: 201 — status PAID, orderNumber present, provider absent,
# paidAt present (byte-for-byte the old contract)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 16 — Setup: hire a second cashier who will never open a session
# @name hireSessionless
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Payments Sessionless Cashier",
  "email": "pay-sessionless-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234583",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 17 — Setup: the sessionless cashier logs in
# @name sessionlessLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireSessionless.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 18 — A valid cashier with NO session opens a gateway slip
# Expected: 409 — session-conflict, "Open a session first."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionlessLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 19 — Setup: hire a SALES_ATTENDANT (the title-gate persona)
# @name hireAttendant
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Payments Attendant",
  "email": "pay-attendant-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234584",
  "jobTitle": "SALES_ATTENDANT"
}

### 20 — Setup: the attendant logs in
# @name attendantLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireAttendant.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 21 — The attendant opens a gateway slip — the title gate refuses
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{attendantLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 22 — Setup: the seat admin enrolls a customer
# @name enroll
# Expected: 201 (200 on a later re-run — idempotent enroll)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Payments Shopper",
  "phone": "+2348093030381"
}

### 23 — Walk-in with an attached customer: the slip rides their identity
# Expected: 202 — customerPublicId = the enrolled customer's publicId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK",
  "customerPhone": "08093030381"
}

### 24 — A well-formed phone nobody has enrolled
# Expected: 400 — "No customer with phone ... Enroll them first."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK",
  "customerPhone": "+2348099990081"
}

### 25 — An empty basket with a provider
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 26 — Anonymous gateway checkout — no token at all
# Expected: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 27 — CARD + MONNIFY — Monnify is the transfer rail
# Expected: 400 — detail mentions bank transfer (use TRANSFER with MONNIFY)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentProvider": "MONNIFY"
}
